# Backend Dockerfile Patterns

## Base Image

Always use `python:3.11-slim`:

```dockerfile
FROM python:3.11-slim
```

## System Dependencies

Install PostgreSQL client libraries:

```dockerfile
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y \
    gcc \
    g++ \
    libpq-dev \
    postgresql-client \
    curl \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*
```

## UV Installation

Install `uv` for fast package management:

```dockerfile
RUN curl -LsSf https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/releases/latest/download/uv-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz | \
    tar -xz -C /tmp && \
    find /tmp -name "uv" -type f -executable -exec mv {} /usr/local/bin/uv \; && \
    chmod +x /usr/local/bin/uv && \
    rm -rf /tmp/uv* && \
    uv --version
```

## Dependency Installation

**Extract dependencies from pyproject.toml and install (NO editable install):**

```dockerfile
COPY backend/pyproject.toml /app/pyproject.toml
COPY backend/ /app

RUN cd /app && python -c "import tomllib; f=open('pyproject.toml','rb'); d=tomllib.load(f); deps=d['project']['dependencies']; import subprocess; subprocess.run(['uv', 'pip', 'install', '--system', '--no-cache'] + deps, check=True)"
```

## Startup Script

Create startup script that waits for database:

```dockerfile
RUN echo '#!/bin/bash\n\
echo "Waiting for TimescaleDB database..."\n\
until PGPASSWORD=${DB_PASS} psql -h ${DB_HOST} -U ${DB_USER} -d ${DB_NAME} -c "SELECT 1" > /dev/null 2>&1; do\n\
  echo "Database not ready, waiting..."\n\
  sleep 2\n\
done\n\
echo "Database is ready!"\n\
exec uvicorn main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 --reload\n\
' > /app/start.sh && chmod +x /app/start.sh
```

## Important Notes

- **Never use `-e .` (editable install)** in Docker - install dependencies only
- Copy `pyproject.toml` before source code for better caching
- Use `--system --no-cache` flags with `uv pip install`
- Wait for database before starting application
- Use `--reload` flag for development hot-reload
